# KnowMe CareerForge MDC Rules (Cursor)

When activated for career positioning, resume tailoring, or repo-to-resume analysis:

1. **Evidence-First Invariant**: Enforce strict L1~L3 evidence classification (see `references/01-evidence-mining.md`). Never hallucinate ungrounded revenue metrics, fake degrees, or false tenures.
2. **Repo-to-Resume Extraction**: Extract codebase facts using `python3 scripts/evidence/extract-evidence.py --repo .` or execute the one-shot pipeline `python3 scripts/pipeline/forge.py`.
3. **Target Alignment & JD Parsing**: Analyze target Job Descriptions using `python3 scripts/evidence/analyze-jd.py` (see `references/03-jd-analysis.md`).
4. **Template Search**: Match template via `python3 scripts/template/search-template.py "<Target Role>"` (see `references/04-template-selection.md`).
5. **HTML Canvas Editing**: Edit exclusively in `workspace/resume.html` Intermediate Working Canvas (`scripts/template/instantiate-resume.py`). Calibrate CSS variables (`--resume-*`) in `:root` (see `references/05-html-canvas-tokens.md`).
6. **Dual QA & Deterministic PDF**: Validate layout height ($297\text{mm} \le 1122.5\text{px}$) and ATS via `python3 scripts/validation/validate-resume.py`. Export final vector PDF via `python3 scripts/rendering/render-pdf.py`.
7. **Quiet Execution Protocol**: Execute all tools silently with `--quiet`. Never output raw HTML/CSS into the chat. Deliver concise value proposition and direct output file paths.
8. **Authoritative Guide**: Refer to root `AGENT.md` for Vercel-inspired editorial standards and `ARCHITECTURE.md` for system design.
